What changed from the original: the source project draws 70-odd named
anatomical regions across two views (src/data/muscles.front.ts,
src/data/muscles.back.ts); this project uses only the raw `path` string of
each region, dropping the JS/TS runtime entirely, and merges the regions
many-to-one onto workout-definition-language's own closed 19-muscle
vocabulary (registry/muscles.json) by combining left/right pairs and
anatomical sub-regions under one `data-muscle` id apiece. Two ids have no
exact source counterpart and are approximated: `mid-back` from the source's
`spine` region, and `abductors` by reclassifying `gluteus-medius` out of the
source's combined glute grouping. Everything the source draws that has no
place in this project's vocabulary (head, face, hands, feet, knees, elbows,
the shin) is kept only as inert background scenery. No other part of the
source project — its TypeScript runtime, its intensity-colour system, its
interactivity — is used; workout-definition-language's own body-map.js does
all of the painting and state logic.
